<title>USA: Alexion gets retroviral vectors patent.</title>
<headline>Alexion gets retroviral vectors patent.</headline>
<dateline>NEW HAVEN, Conn. 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alexion Pharmaceuticals Inc said it received a U.S. patent for its retroviral vector particles.</p>
<p>Alexion's patent claim says the retroviral vector particles, or proteins, act as a resistent shell to the human immune system. Developed in conjuction with its Swiss partner, Novartis AG &quot;The shell allows us to deliver cancer fighting gene therapy designed by Novartis, to the afflicted areas,&quot; said Leonard Bell, President and CEO of Alexion.</p>
<p>Alexion estimates the gene therapy will help 400,000 to 500,000 cancer patients. It recieved patent number 5,643,770.</p>
</text>
